PATCH 323: fix the three mission-render BASE-LOSSES the now-iterating 459a loop (patch 322) reaches for
the first time -- so the mission survives past c452=1 into sustained per-frame iteration.

With patch 322 the 22dd render script advances (41df no longer traps), so 459a's OUTER loop runs to
completion and re-enters via patch-295's pump -> c452 advances.  Each new frame drives the mission PAINT
walk (206f->209e) and the 22dd script into functions never before executed, exposing three Ghidra
base-losses that SIGSEGV on the default build (mission-path only; the 24 menu flows never reach them).
All asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin, DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00.

(1) FUN_1000_a722 (asm 0x1a733, mission HUD text method, reached via 79f5 when (d548&0x7f)==3 -- a state
    the iterating render now enters): `mov di,[0x6d34]; mov ax,[di+0x26]` -- di=word[DGROUP:0x6d34] is the
    player-vehicle node NEAR OFFSET (0xc05c); Ghidra's DAT_2000_2d34 macro is *(int**) so
    `DAT_2000_2d34 + 0x26` deref'd (int*)0xc05c + 0x98 as a host address -> SIGSEGV.  Rebase: read the
    near-offset word and index g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)(vn+0x26).

(2) FUN_0000_3a0f (asm 0x3a0f, reticle-draw 22dd script handler): bx=word[0x156a] is the dst-geom NEAR
    OFFSET (Ghidra DAT_1000_d56a is *(int**) -> host-ptr deref -> SIGSEGV) -> rebase g_mem+0x1c000+
    (uint16)off for the [bx+6/0xa/0xe/8/0xf/0xc] reads.  Second base-loss: the reticle method dispatch
    `mov ax,[0x1550]; si=ax&7; ax^=si; si+=si; mov si,cs:[si+0x3a52]; mov bx,0x6c16; lcall [si]` -- the
    CS-image method-vector table @0x3a52 = {0x6b4,0x6b8,0x6bc,0x6c0,0x6c8,0x6cc,0x6d0,0x6d4} (DGROUP
    far-vector offsets; [0x6b4]=MGAVIDEO 26a1 sprite/box blit); Ghidra read the table at host address
    0x3a52 (wild) and dropped ax/bx.  Rebase the table read to g_mem+0x3a52 and the vector to the DGROUP
    far-ptr; thread 26a1(ax,0,0,bx=0x6c16,0) per the patch-305 convention (0x6c16 = the DAT_2000_2c16..
    reticle rect this fn just populated).

(3) FUN_0000_3fbf (asm 0x3fbf, crosshair/reticle PLOT, called by 3a0f) -- the near-twin of the already-
    reconstructed FUN_0000_3fba (patch 194) but WITHOUT the cursor advance: si=word[0x1552] /
    di=word[0x156a] are dst/src geom NEAR OFFSETS (Ghidra int* / int** -> host-ptr deref -> SIGSEGV);
    the plot address is rowtab[cx]+dx inside the page-seg es=word[word[0x156a]].  Rebased onto
    g_mem+0x1c000 exactly as 3fba; plot es:[di] (page-seg<<4); the je branch far-calls [0x159c]/[0x15a0].

RESULT (default `make native`, mission ACCEPT path BATTLES(160,100)->OK(205,128)->ACCEPT(40,186)): the
459a loop iterates -- under the fast cooperative tick (FIST_COOP_TICK) c452 climbs 1 -> 314, op 0x24 (the
windshield-render post) re-posts, and the mission FB CHANGES frame-to-frame (op-0x24 post #1 vs #2 differ
by AE=209 px = the advancing HUD/radar sim).  Default (25000 Hz SIGALRM) is crash-free (3/3 exit 124 =
spins, no core).  NEXT BLOCKER PINNED: the render script then reaches the unregistered handler 0x3a68 (the
reticle-GRATICULE loop: iterator [0x1630] over di=0x6bbe + 3a92 line-draw + 3d4c) -> traps to a no-op ->
cursor freezes at c452=314 (the same 41df class, but its [0x1630] list iterator also floods op 0x1c and
needs its own reconstruction) -- the pinned next step for sustained iteration.

MISSION-PATH ONLY (a722 is a d548-gated HUD method; 3a0f/3fbf are 22dd render-script handlers reached only
inside the in-mission 459a loop) -> strictly behaviour-neutral for the 24 menu/pre-mission verify flows.
Sources stay pristine (re_out/fist.c 61453e42); patched via build/.

